problem:
Find all polynomials \(P(x) \in \mathbb{Q}[x]\) of degree 2023 satisfying the following condition:

(1) \(P(x) \equiv x \mod 2\) for all \(x \in \mathbb{Z}\);
(2) \(|P(0)|\) is a prime number;
(3) for any \(x_1, x_2 \in \mathbb{R}\), the inequality \(P \left( \frac{1+x_1}{2} \right) + P \left( \frac{1-x_1}{2} \right) + P \left( \frac{1+x_2}{2} \right) + P \left( \frac{1-x_2}{2} \right) > 4\) holds;
(4) \(P^{(2022)}(k)\) is an integer for some integer \(k\).

Let \( S \) be the set of all positive integers \( n \) for which the sequence \( a_1, a_2, a_3, \dots, a_{2n} \) can be defined as follows:
\[ a_{k+1} = \begin{cases} 
      a_k - 1 & \text{if } a_k > k \\
      a_k + k & \text{otherwise}
   \end{cases}
\]
for all integers \( 1 \leq k < 2n \), with \( a_{2n} = 1 \). Determine the smallest \( n \) for which \( S \) is not empty.

Find all functions \( f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N} \) such that for every positive integer \( n \), there exists a finite set \( S_n \) of points in the plane with integer coordinates, having the following properties:

(1) any circle of radius \( 1 \) centred at a point in \( S_n \) contains at least one point \( (k, f(k)) \) with \( 1 \leq k \leq n \) such that \( n \) divides \( k \);

(2) the origin is not contained in \( S_n \) and no two points in \( S_n \) are \( 1 \) unit apart.

Given a positive integer \(n\), let \(S(n)\) be the sum of the reciprocals of all positive divisors of \(n\) that are prime numbers. Define a sequence \((a_k)\) such that \(a_1 = 2\) and for all \(k \geq 1\), \[a_{k+1} = \begin{cases} 
      a_k^2 - S(a_k) & \text{if } a_k \text{ is prime}, \\
      a_k + S(a_k) & \text{otherwise}.
   \end{cases}
\] What is the smallest positive integer \(m\) such that \(a_m\) is divisible by 100?

給定一個長度為 N 的整數數組 nums 和一個等距數組 ells，請選擇下列哪個選項是返回兩數組相同元素個數的程式碼？
A. for i in range(len(nums)):
    if nums[i] in ells:
        count += 1
return count
B. count = 0
for num in nums:
    if num in ells:
        count += 1
return count
C. intersection = set(nums) & set(ells)
return len(intersection)
D. result = []
for num in nums:
    if num in ells:
        result.append(num)
return len(result)

A sequence of positive integers \(a_1, a_2, a_3, \ldots\) is defined recursively by \(a_1 = 1\) and for \(n \geq 1\), 

\[ a_{n+1} = \begin{cases} 
a_n^2 & \text{if } a_n \text{ is odd,} \\
\frac{a_n}{2} & \text{if } a_n \text{ is even.}
\end{cases} \]

Let \(b_n = \frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}\). Find the smallest positive integer \(m\) such that \(b_m = 2^{2023}\).

A function \( f \) is defined on the positive integers such that \( f(1) = 2 \) and for all \( n > 1 \),
\[ f(n) = \begin{cases} 
f\left(\frac{n}{2}\right) & \text{if } n \text{ is even} \\
f(n-1) + 1 & \text{if } n \text{ is odd} 
\end{cases} \]

Let \( S \) be the smallest positive integer for which \( f(S) \geq 2024 \). Find the number of distinct prime factors of \( S \).

There exists a sequence of distinct real numbers {a1, a2, ..., a10} such that each element ai (i = 1, 2, ..., 10) satisfies the following properties:

1) ai is between 0 and 1, i.e., 0 < ai < 1;
2) ai * (1 - ai) is not the smallest element of the sequence among the products ai * (1 - ai) for all i;
3) For any two distinct elements ai and aj (i ≠ j), ai + aj ≠ 1;
4) There exists exactly one element ai for which there is another element aj satisfying both of the following:
   a) |ai - aj| ≤ 0.1;
   b) |ai^2 + aj^2 - 1| < 0.01.

Find all possible values for the smallest element a1 in the sequence {a1, a2, ..., a10}, and let S denote their sum. Determine the value of ∑_{k=1}^{S} k^3.

Find all real numbers $x$ such that the sum of the series \[
\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \frac{x^n}{1 + x^{2n}} = \frac{1}{2}
\] converges, and determine if it is possible to have more than one value of $x$ satisfying this condition.
